{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Gerrit change 2689, and a correction I am recording rather than quietly fixing\n\n`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2689` — \"Gzip the user-data so terraform can plan\nagain\", `rebar-ticket: a68c-9633-248c-4b06`, DCO signed. NOT submitted.\n\n**Patchset 1 was pushed on a misread of `make verify`, and should not have been.** The run\nfinished `2 failed, 19842 passed, 80 skipped, 7 errors` and I read the harness's wrapper exit\ncode as the verdict instead of the pytest summary. Recording it because the standard I was given\nwas \"prove by measurement, not plausibility\", and I briefly did the opposite with my own gate.\n\nThe two failures were REAL and were mine:\n\n```\nFAILED tests/scripts/test_check_import_walk.py::TestScriptsLeg::test_real_scripts_leg_passes\n  - check_user_data_size.py: ModuleNotFoundError\nFAILED tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py::\n  test_every_sibling_import_under_scripts_is_preceded_by_a_path_insert\n```\n\n`scripts/check_user_data_size.py` imports its sibling `check_templatefile_escapes` (deliberately —\nthat module already resolves `templatefile()` call sites and their variable maps, and duplicating\nthat logic would be worse). But `scripts/` is not a package, so a bare sibling import resolves\nonly while that directory is on `sys.path`. It is under `python scripts/<x>.py`, which is why\n`make lint` was green, and it is during a FULL test session because `tests/scripts/conftest.py`\ninserts it process-wide. It is NOT under an importlib load or a subset run. That is exactly bug\n`291e-7b48-3f24-41c6`'s class, and the repo has a standing guard for it that caught me.\n\nFixed in patchset 2 with the `sys.path.insert` the convention requires, derived from `__file__`\nso it holds under every invocation style, with a comment saying why. Re-ran the two failing\nmodules plus my own: **27 passed**.\n\n**The other 7 were self-inflicted noise, not defects:** every one was\n`Failed: The repo HEAD moved during this test (84ef284833 -> e8426ab316)` — I committed while\n`make verify` was running, and a family of tests asserts HEAD stability. My mistake in procedure,\nnot a finding. The re-run is against a quiescent tree.\n\n## What the verify run did establish\n\n19,842 tests passed in 52m53s. `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean on the amended tree\n(mypy: no issues in 767 source files). The mechanism-delta ratchet initially refused the new gate\nas an unjustified `ci_gate` and now admits it via a `mechanism-ok` marker at the definition site\nnaming this bug.\n\n## Vote state\n\nAwaiting `LLM-Review` and `Verified` on 2689. Not submitted, and this ticket stays `in_progress`\nuntil it is `Verified +1` — a passing plan review is not a substitute for green CI.\n\nThe plan-review attestation is **certified** (third round; the first two BLOCKed on AC3 naming no\nproving method, then on the deferred boot check having no back-out — both fixed in the plan\nrather than argued away)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788650460824299001,"uuid":"c137d2d1-a387-4e95-b899-20c62e132396"}